    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4518",
      "problem": "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130155/assets/76fbe25754bbca564d39872ef9817754c49a8af7b14c55663d87e416e17e5ac0.svg)\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130155/assets/9867975d7c037dfc9f9dc3f3a97a54d4616968fa065dab2eb7df63092f9fc42e.svg)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130155/assets/3f8d3bbb7bd1bba7c64651844edfbd41049ffc8ce5465b1146352cf8d304b13f.svg)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130155/assets/711c76f79af405029bb73a1120d8bdf588efcc2085f4262af0153e7cc648b105.svg)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130155/assets/498541b430e0f3a2f31ae928c91775b7c0264de34e46f3348785e9afbc893b30.svg)\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$",
